    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18273" root="زنو" body-key="z">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زنّى عَلَيْهِ</span></b>  <i>He straitened,</i> or <i>oppressed, him;
made strait,</i> or <i>close, to him:</i> (ISd, K:) it occurs
thus, without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>, by poetic license, for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَنَّأَ</span>, in a
saying of a rájiz cited in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شدخ</span>, as an ex. of
the word <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَادِخَةٌ</span>. (S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زنأ</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زنّى</span> also
signifies <i>He</i> (a man) <i>became lax in his joints.</i>
(TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زن</span>.)

